            "role": "user"
          },
          "create_time": 1730642400.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Can you explain the product rule using x^2 * sin(x)? I have a calculus exam on Friday."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "msg-01-1": {
        "id": "msg-01-1",
        "parent": "msg-01-0",
        "children": [
          "msg-01-2"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-01-1",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1730642440.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The product rule says (fg)' = f'g + fg'. With f = x^2 and g = sin(x): 2x*sin(x) + x^2*cos(x)."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "msg-01-2": {
        "id": "msg-01-2",
        "parent": "msg-01-1",
        "children": [
          "msg-01-3"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-01-2",
          "author": {
            "role": "user"
          },
          "create_time": 1730642480.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Thanks, can you give me two more practice problems?"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "msg-01-3": {
        "id": "msg-01-3",
        "parent": "msg-01-2",
        "children": [],
        "message": {
          "id": "msg-01-3",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          "create_time": 1730642520.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Try differentiating x*e^x and (x^3)*ln(x), then check against the product rule."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
